{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "LUK",
  "chapter": 23,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the whole multitude of them arose, and led him to Pilate.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they began to accuse him, saying, We found this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perverting the nation, and forbidding to give tribute to Cesar, saying, that he himself is Christ a king.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pilate asked him, saying, Art thou the King of the Jews? And he answered him and said, Thou sayest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said Pilate to the chief priests, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the people, I find no fault in this man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they were the more fierce, saying, He stirreth up the people, teaching throughout all Judea, beginning from Galilee to this place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Pilate heard of Galilee, he asked whether the man was a Galilean.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as soon as he knew that he belonged to Herod's jurisdiction, he sent him to Herod, who himself was also at Jerusalem at that time.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when Herod saw Jesus, he was exceeding glad: for he had been for a long time, desirous to see him, because he had heard many things of him; and he hoped to see some miracle done by him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he questioned with him in many words; but he answered him nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the chief priests and scribes stood and vehemently accused him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Herod with his troops set him at naught, and mocked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and arrayed him in a gorgeous robe, and sent him again to Pilate.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the same day Pilate and Herod were made friends together; for before they were at enmity between themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pilate, when he had called together the chief priests, and the rulers, and the people,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Said to them, Ye have brought this man to me, as one that perverteth the people: and behold, I, having examined ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before you, have found no fault in this man, touching those things of which ye accuse him;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "No, nor yet Herod: for I sent you to him; and lo, nothing worthy of death is done to him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will therefore chastise him, and release ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For of necessity he must release one to them at the feast.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they cried out all at once, saying, Away with this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and release to us Barabbas:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Who, for a certain sedition made in the city, and for murder, was cast into prison.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pilate therefore, willing to release Jesus, spoke again to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But they cried, saying, Crucify, crucify him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to them the third time, Why, what evil hath he done? I have found no cause of death in him; I will therefore chastise him, and let ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " go.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they were urgent with loud voices, requiring that he might be crucified: and the voices of them, and of the chief priests prevailed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pilate gave sentence that it should be as they required.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he released to them him that for sedition and murder had been cast into prison, whom they had desired; but he delivered Jesus to their will.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as they led him away, they laid hold upon one Simon a Cyrenian, coming out of the country, and on him they laid the cross, that he might bear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " after Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there followed him a great company of people, and of women, who also bewailed and lamented him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Jesus turning to them, said, Daughters of Jerusalem, weep not for me, but weep for yourselves, and for your children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For behold, the days are coming, in which they shall say, Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the barren, and the wombs that never bore, and the breasts which never nourished infants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then shall they begin to say to the mountains, Fall on us; and to the hills, Cover us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if they do these things in a green tree, what will be done in the dry?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And two others, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " malefactors, were led with him to be put to death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they had come to the place which is called Calvary, there they crucified him, and the malefactors; one on the right hand, and the other on the left.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said Jesus, Father, forgive them: for they know not what they do. And they parted his raiment, and cast lots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the people stood beholding. And the rulers also with them derided ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", saying, He saved others; let him save himself, if he is Christ the chosen of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the soldiers also mocked him, coming to him, and offering him vinegar,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And saying, If thou art the King of the Jews, save thyself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And a superscription also was written over him, in letters of Greek, and Latin, and Hebrew, THIS IS THE KING OF THE JEWS.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And one of the malefactors, who were hanged, railed on him, saying, If thou art Christ, save thyself and us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the other answering, rebuked him, saying, Dost not thou fear God, seeing thou art in the same condemnation?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And we indeed justly; for we receive the due reward of our deeds: but this man hath done nothing amiss.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to Jesus, Lord, remember me when thou comest into thy kingdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus said to him, Verily I say to thee, This day shalt thou be with me in paradise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it was about the sixth hour, and there was a darkness over all the land until the ninth hour.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the sun was darkened, and the vail of the temple was rent in the midst.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when Jesus had cried with a loud voice, he said, Father, into thy hands I commend my spirit: and having said thus, he expired.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now when the centurion saw what was done, he glorified God, saying, Certainly this was a righteous man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all the people that came together to that sight, beholding the things which were done, smote their breasts, and returned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all his acquaintance, and the women that followed him from Galilee, stood afar off beholding these things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a man named Joseph, a counselor: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and he was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a good man, and a just:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(The same had not consented to the counsel and deed of them) ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Arimathea, a city of the Jews; who also himself waited for the kingdom of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " went to Pilate, and begged the body of Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.53",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.53",
      "verse": 53,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took it down, and wrapped it in linen, and laid it in a sepulcher that was hewn in stone, in which man was never before laid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.54",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.54",
      "verse": 54,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And that day was the preparation, and the sabbath drew on.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.55",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.55",
      "verse": 55,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the women also, who came with him from Galilee, followed after, and beheld the sepulcher, and how his body was laid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.23.56",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.23.56",
      "verse": 56,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they returned, and prepared spices and ointments; and rested on the sabbath, according to the commandment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
